course: dictionary
lesson: 3914
title: Frog: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean different things in different places. Look at the words around it to find the meaning the writer wants. «A frog can take in some oxygen through its thin, moist skin.» Here frog is an animal, because it has skin and breathes.
explain: The same word can also be part of a phrase, and a phrase often means something different from its single words. «A frog in my throat» has nothing to do with an animal. It means your voice sounds croaky, as if you need to clear it before you speak.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right. Frog is a noun, so it names a thing, and frogs is the plural: more than one frog.
fact: A frog is a small green or brown animal with long back legs that jumps and lives near water.
fact: Frogs are amphibians: tadpoles hatch from eggs and grow into frogs.
fact: «Frog spawn» is the name for the eggs that frogs lay in water.
fact: «Many frogs catch insects with a long, sticky tongue.»
fact: «A frog in your throat» means a croaky voice.
exercise: «Many frogs catch insects with a long, sticky tongue.» What do many frogs use to catch insects? | Their back legs only | Their thin, moist skin | Their loud voices | *A long, sticky tongue
exercise: Dad says, «I've got a frog in my throat.» What does he mean? | He has an animal stuck in his mouth | He wants to jump high | He is going swimming | *His voice sounds croaky
exercise: «A frog needs two habitats: its tadpoles live in water.» Find and copy one word that means a home for living things. | needs | *habitats | frog | tadpoles
test: Tadpoles live in water and breathe with what? | Their mouths | *Gills | Their tails | Their long back legs
test: Which phrase means a croaky voice? | «Leap frog» | «Frogs on every continent» | «Frog spawn» | *«A frog in my throat»
exam: Which sentence uses frog as an animal, not as part of a phrase? | «Frog spawn is in the pond» | «Leap frog is my favourite game» | «A frog in my throat» | *«Frogs live on every continent except Antarctica»
